DECISION (judge fable-5.1-xhigh 2026-09-08T03:48Z): defer. Do not build the `judge_only` gate yet.

Evidence (live seat ledgers, this run):
```
$ for f in ~/workspaces/agent-state/lanes/seats/*alibaba*.json; do ...; done
alibaba-coding__qwen3.8-max.json    {"health_class":"rate_limited","consecutive_failure_count":4,"usable_at":"2026-09-14T16:14:00.051Z"}
alibaba-coding__qwen3.8-flash.json  {"health_class":"rate_limited","consecutive_failure_count":2,"usable_at":"2026-09-14T16:14:00.316Z"}
alibaba-coding__qwen3.7-max.json    {"health_class":"rate_limited","consecutive_failure_count":3,"usable_at":"2026-09-14T16:14:00.344Z"}
alibaba-coding__qwen3.7-plus.json   {"health_class":"rate_limited","consecutive_failure_count":2,"usable_at":"2026-09-14T16:14:00.666Z"}
alibaba-coding__glm-5.2.json        {"health_class":"rate_limited","consecutive_failure_count":1,"usable_at":"2026-09-14T16:14:00.470Z"}
(+ deepseek-v4-flash-0731, deepseek-v4-pro — same wall)
```

All seven alibaba-coding seats are rate_limited until 2026-09-14T16:14Z — six days out, the whole provider, not one model. qwen3.8-max also fast-died in the last 3h of watch.log.

So the mechanism this issue asks for would activate a judge seat that `find_senior_seat` still could not draw, because `seat_usable` fails on the wall independently of cap. Building it now buys nothing until 2026-09-14 and adds a filter-chain branch to `pick_seat` that no live caller exercises — deletion-first says not yet. The current senior ladder is unaffected and healthy: `senior_seats_in_order` = cursor/cursor-grok-4.6-high, xai-oauth/grok-4.6, openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731.

The re-scope of #4445 (alibaba parked at cap 0, qwen3.8-max declared but inert) is correct and stands as-is. Re-open this as agent-ready ON or AFTER 2026-09-14T16:14Z, and only if a smoke of alibaba-coding/qwen3.8-max returns OK at that point — if the provider is still walled or dies on smoke, close it instead. Removing needs-orchestrator; no orchestrator question remains.
